    "message": "Fix preparation-stage LLM calls and ledger freezes\n\nAll four initial-condition AI calls failed live with Opus 5.5:\n\n- Thinking cannot be disabled on Opus, and thinking tokens count toward\n  max_tokens, so small caps returned thinking only. The router now adds 4,096\n  tokens of thinking headroom (and reserves its cost) outside runtime, and\n  preparation calls request effort \"low\".\n- Initial-needs and scenario-draft answer caps were below the size of a valid\n  answer; raise them to measured per-profile sizes.\n- The output validator did not resolve Pydantic \"$ref\", so the Web scenario\n  text parse failed for every reply. Support $ref/$defs, oneOf, const, typed\n  additionalProperties, exclusive bounds, minLength and pattern.\n- Web-search usage sums several sampling passes, exceeding the single-pass\n  reservation and freezing the machine-wide campaign ledger. Reserve\n  max_tokens x (searches + 1).\n- Add `sheltersim usage --unfreeze ID --confirm ID --reason TEXT` to re-open a\n  frozen ledger. The ledger stays schema v1; the event is audited in a\n  separate usage-audit file so older readers keep working.\n- Warn on stderr when `prepare` falls back to rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
